mmended B earlier and haven't changed. Now we need to produce a public message that references the discussion, uses explicit facts, and state our current recommendation. We can either maintain B or shift. Let's evaluate again: B's strengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Weaknesses: pretentious, wrong tone, grumpy, uncooperative, weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks. A's strengths: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. C's strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership. Weaknesses: unfriendly, not open to new ideas, not good at taking criticism, unorganized, show-off, eats unhealthily. D's strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: hot temper, know-it-all, weak leadership, moody, loner, arrogant.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best balances criteria. B has strong reliability and stress handling, but crew cooperation issues are severe. A has strong decision and calmness, but communication and egocentric may affect crew. C has strong situational awareness and leadership, but crew cooperation issues also severe. D has problem solving and responsibility, but temperament issues.\n\nWhich is best? The panel hasn't converged. As agent_3, we can either maintain B or shift. We need to provide reasoning. Let's consider the weight: reliability and stress handling are critical. B is very conscientious (reliability) and handles stress well. A's reliability is not explicit. C's reliability unknown. D's reliability unknown. So B has clear reliability evidence. Communication issues are serious but can be mitigated. A's communication difficulty and egocentric also serious. C's unfriendly also serious. So B may still be best.\n\nThus we keep vote for B. Provide public message: \"I still recommend B, because reliability and stress handling are paramount, and B's technical competence is strong, while communication issues can be addressed.\" Use explicit facts: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills; concerns: pretentious, wrong tone, grumpy, uncooperative, weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks. Compare to A's egocentric and not willing to further education, and C's unfriendly and not open to new ideas. Conclude B is best.\n\nNow produce output: PUBLIC_MESSAGE with that content, then METADATA_JSON with agent \"agent_3\" and vote \"Candidate B\". Ensure format exactly as required."}
