didate C, Agent 3 (Sofia) recommended Candidate B. Now we need to produce a contribution as Agent 1. Our current vote is Candidate C (as per shared mental model). We need to respond to the latest contributions: Agent 2's recommendation of A, Agent 3's recommendation of B, and our own earlier recommendation of C. We need to either maintain C or shift. We need to provide evidence from our notes: Candidate C can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, regarded as a show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Also we have that C is sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Also we have that C is regarded as a show\u2011off. Also we have that C is not open to new ideas. Also we have that C is unfriendly. Also we have that C has very good leadership qualities. Also we have that C can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision.\n\nWe need to compare to A and B. A: quick correct decisions, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, pretentious tone, grumpy, uncooperative, weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks.\n\nWe need to argue for C, referencing the discussion. We can say that while A has quick decisions and calmness, the lack of willingness to further education and egocentric attitude raise concerns about adaptability and crew cooperation. B has strong reliability and stress handling but serious crew cooperation issues (pretentious, uncooperative, nasty remarks). C, on the other hand, brings unique safety-critical strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, and strong leadership, which are crucial for l